# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: an error is displayed wherever it happens -- inline, in a `,`
#         arm, in a detach() body; a failure in one top-level task does
#         not disturb another; an error in sequential code stops the
#         rest of its block; a detached failure does not.
# matrix-row: separator-detach
#
# Rewritten from legacy tests/2.x/detach-error.chk for the host driver,
# whose clock is virtual, so the "does not impact other top-level tasks"
# case is ordered by advance-clock rather than by a real sleep.  The
# diagnostic text is this core's (`LookupError: slot access: ...`), not
# the legacy `input.u:@.1: lookup failed: f`; the legacy `called from:`
# backtrace lines have no counterpart.
#
# `,` detaches its LEFT arm, so in `f, 0` the failing lookup is the
# detached strand, reported through the diag hook, and `0` is the
# chunk's value.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var x = 0
## host: run f
## host: run f, 0
## host: run detach(f); 0
## host: step 1000
## host: run { sleep(500ms); f }, { sleep(1s); x = 1 }
## host: step 1000
## host: advance-clock 500
## host: step 1000
## host: run x
## host: advance-clock 500
## host: step 1000
## host: run x
## host: run { f ; x = 2 }
## host: run x
## host: run { detach(f) ; x = 3 }; 0
## host: step 1000
## host: run x
## host: run x = 0
## host: run detach { f ; x = 4 }; 0
## host: step 1000
## host: run x
## host: run detach { detach(f) ; x = 5 }; 0
## host: step 1000
## host: run x
[00000000] 0
[00000000] !!! LookupError: slot access: slot 'f' not found
[00000000] !!! LookupError: slot access: slot 'f' not found
[00000000] 0
[00000000] !!! LookupError: slot access: slot 'f' not found
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
